  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{D}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{D(t)-D(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=4.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{\u2032}(4) & \u2248\\frac{D(4)-D(4-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{D(4)-D(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{19-14}{1} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $t=4$ is $5$ hundreds per year.",
